<title>GREECE: GREEK DIPLOMATS PURSUE STRIKE OVER TAX CHANGE.</title>
<headline>GREEK DIPLOMATS PURSUE STRIKE OVER TAX CHANGE.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek diplomats said on Monday they would continue a strike for the second consecutive working day to protest against a new tax on their spending money while they serve abroad.</p>
<p>Most foreign ministry employees in Athens also stayed away from work because the issue concerns both serving diplomats and administrative personnel, a ministry source said.</p>
<p>The diplomats are deciding on a day-by-day basis whether to continue the strike.</p>
<p>--Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
